The FACTS in `records/` come from public datasets that keep their own terms:

  Census of Governments, 2022
    U.S. Census Bureau. US Government work; public domain.
    https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/gus/datasets/2022/govt_units_2022.ZIP

  TIGERweb
    U.S. Census Bureau geography. US Government work; public domain.
    Boundaries are referenced by URL (see `boundaries.geojson_url`), never copied
    into this repository.

  unitedstates/congress-legislators
    CC0-1.0. https://github.com/unitedstates/congress-legislators

  openstates/people
    CC0-1.0. https://github.com/openstates/people

  global-law corpus
    Referenced by path and pinned commit only. No law text is copied into this
    repository; read the corpus and its own NOTICE at the pinned commit.

CC0 places the datasets in the public domain. Where a dataset says otherwise, its
term wins for the rows that came from it, and the record's `license` field says
which one applied.
